\section*{Question 4}

Let \(R\) be the region bounded by the graphs of \(y=\sqrt{x}\) and \(y=\frac{x}{2}\), as shown in the figure above.
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] Find the area of \(R\).
\item[(b)] The region \(R\) is the base of a solid. For this solid, the cross sections perpendicular to the \(x\)-axis are squares. Find the volume of this solid.
\item[(c)] Write, but do not evaluate, an integral expression for the volume of the solid generated when \(R\) is rotated about the horizontal line \(y=2\).
\end{itemize}
![](https://cdn.mathpix.com/cropped/d859b347-7a22-46e6-92c2-32ebe8eba545-1.jpg?height=466&width=696&top_left_y=391&top_left_x=1186)
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] Area \(=\int_{0}^{4}\left(\sqrt{x}-\frac{x}{2}\right) d x=\frac{2}{3} x^{3 / 2}-\left.\frac{x^{2}}{4}\right|_{x=0} ^{x=4}=\frac{4}{3}\)
\item[(b)] Volume \(=\int_{0}^{4}\left(\sqrt{x}-\frac{x}{2}\right)^{2} d x=\int_{0}^{4}\left(x-x^{3 / 2}+\frac{x^{2}}{4}\right) d x\)
\[
=\frac{x^{2}}{2}-\frac{2 x^{5 / 2}}{5}+\left.\frac{x^{3}}{12}\right|_{x=0} ^{x=4}=\frac{8}{15}
\]
\item[(c)] Volume \(=\pi \int_{0}^{4}\left(\left(2-\frac{x}{2}\right)^{2}-(2-\sqrt{x})^{2}\right) d x\)
\end{itemize}
\(3:\left\{\begin{array}{l}1: \text { integrand } \\ 1: \text { antiderivative } \\ 1: \text { answer }\end{array}\right.\)
